","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qd5","uci":"d4d5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/5ppp/p2p4/1ppQ4/4P3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 1 9","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Be6","uci":"c8e6","fen":"r2qkbnr/5ppp/p2pb3/1ppQ4/4P3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 2 10","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qc6+","uci":"d5c6","fen":"r2qkbnr/5ppp/p1Qpb3/1pp5/4P3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 3 10","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bd7","uci":"e6d7","fen":"r2qkbnr/3b1ppp/p1Qp4/1pp5/4P3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 4 11","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Qd5","uci":"c6d5","fen":"r2qkbnr/3b1ppp/p2p4/1ppQ4/4P3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 5 11","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"c4","uci":"c5c4","fen":"r2qkbnr/3b1ppp/p2p4/1p1Q4/2p1P3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 12","arrows":[],"highlights":[]}],"hints":[],"intro":"The pawn on b5 covers a4, and White's own pawns block a2 and c2. If the bishop takes c4, the b5 pawn takes it.","type":"explain"}],"teacherNotes":{"points":["Name matches the Lichess list: Ruy Lopez, Noah's Ark Trap","The idea: White's bishop on b3 has no safe squares because its own pawns and Black's pawns block it","The mistake is 8.Qxd4 (taking back the pawn with the queen)","After ...c5 the queen must move, and ...c4 traps the bishop","Black wins a bishop for two pawns","Black needs to know the pawn moves ...b5 and ...d6 are solid on their own"],"mistakes":["Playing ...c5 before the knights are traded on d4","Forgetting the move ...Be6 which also develops a piece","Missing that c4 attacks the bishop and every exit is closed"],"questions":["Which squares could the bishop on b3 go to? Why does each fail?","Why is 8.Qxd4 a mistake?","What does the pawn on c4 attack?"]}}]},{"id":"04-quick-mate-italian","title":"Trap 3: the quick knight mate","lessons":[{"id":"quick-knight-mate","title":"The quick knight mate (a risky trap)","steps":[{"id":"04-quick-mate-italian/quick-knight-mate/0","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1","introArrows":[],"introHighlights":[],"moves":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nf3","uci":"g1f3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 2","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Bc4","uci":"f1c4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/2B1P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 3 3","arrows":[],"highlights":[]},{"san":"Nd4","uci":"c6d4","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4p3/2BnP3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 4 4","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"c6","to":"d4"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The knight jumps to d4."},{"san":"Nxe5","uci":"f3e5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4N3/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 4","arrows":[{"color":"R","from":"f3","to":"e5"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"White wins a pawn."},{"san":"Qg5","uci":"d8g5","fen":"r1b1kbnr/pppp1ppp/8/4N1q1/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 5","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"g5","to":"e5"},{"color":"G","from":"g5","to":"g2"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The queen attacks the knight on e5 and the pawn on g2."},{"san":"Nxf7","uci":"e5f7","fen":"r1b1kbnr/pppp1Npp/8/6q1/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 5","arrows":[{"color":"R","from":"f7","to":"g5"},{"color":"R","from":"f7","to":"h8"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"White takes again and attacks the queen and the rook. This is the mistake."},{"san":"Qxg2","uci":"g5g2","fen":"r1b1kbnr/pppp1Npp/8/8/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PqP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 6","arrows":[{"color":"G","from":"g2","to":"h1"},{"color":"G","from":"g2","to":"e4"}],"highlights":[],"comment":"The queen takes g2 and attacks the rook on h1."},{"san":"Rf1","uci":"h1f1","fen":"r1b1kbnr/pppp1Npp/8/8/2BnP3/8/PPPP1PqP/RNBQKR2 b Qkq - 1 6","arrows":[],"highlights":[],"comment":"The rook runs."},{"san":"